## c1-px3 | Calc 1 drill: derivatives | maths | 1 | calc1 | c1-px1
quiz 2 | d/dx (5x³) = ?
* 15x²
o 5x²
o 15x³
o 3x²
= Power rule.
> Next

quiz 2 | d/dx (1/x) = ?
* −1/x²
o 1/x²
o ln x
o −1/x
= x⁻¹ → −x⁻².
> Next

quiz 2 | d/dx (e^(3x)) = ?
* 3e^(3x)
o e^(3x)
o e^(3x)/3
o 3xe^(3x)
= Chain rule.
> Next

quiz 3 | d/dx (sin x cos x) = ?
* cos 2x
o −sin 2x
o 1
o sin 2x
= cos²x − sin²x = cos 2x.
> Next

quiz 3 | d/dx (x ln x) = ?
* ln x + 1
o 1/x
o ln x
o x + ln x
= Product rule: ln x + x(1/x).
> Next

quiz 3 | d/dx √(x² + 1) = ?
* x/√(x² + 1)
o 1/(2√(x² + 1))
o 2x√(x² + 1)
o √(2x)
= ½(x² + 1)^(−½)·2x.
> Next

quiz 3 | d/dx tan(2x) = ?
* 2sec²(2x)
o sec²(2x)
o 2tan(2x)
o −2csc²(2x)
= Chain rule on tan.
> Next

quiz 3 | d/dx (eˣ/x) = ?
* eˣ(x − 1)/x²
o eˣ/x²
o eˣ(x + 1)/x²
o eˣ
= Quotient rule.
> Next

quiz 4 | d/dx ln(ln x) = ?
* 1/(x ln x)
o 1/ln x
o ln x/x
o 1/x²
= (1/ln x)·(1/x).
> Next

quiz 4 | d/dx (3^(x²)) = ?
* 2x ln 3 · 3^(x²)
o x² · 3^(x²−1)
o 3^(x²) ln 3
o 2x · 3^(x²)
= a^u differentiates to a^u ln a · u′.
> Next

quiz 3 | Slope of y = x³ − x at x = 0?
* −1
o 0
o 1
o 3
= y′ = 3x² − 1.
> Next

quiz 3 | Where does f(x) = x² − 6x + 5 have its minimum?
* x = 3
o x = 5
o x = 1
o x = −3
= f′ = 2x − 6 = 0.
