## c1-px4 | Calc 1 drill: integrals | maths | 1 | calc1 | c1-px2
quiz 2 | ∫ 4x³ dx = ?
* x⁴ + C
o 12x² + C
o 4x⁴ + C
o x³ + C
= Power rule backwards.
> Next

quiz 2 | ∫ eˣ dx from 0 to 1 = ?
* e − 1
o e
o 1
o e + 1
= [eˣ]₀¹.
> Next

quiz 2 | ∫ sec²x dx = ?
* tan x + C
o sec x + C
o −cot x + C
o sec x tan x + C
= d/dx tan x = sec² x.
> Next

quiz 3 | ∫ 1/(2x + 1) dx = ?
* ½ln|2x + 1| + C
o ln|2x + 1| + C
o 2ln|2x + 1| + C
o 1/(2x + 1)² + C
= Divide by the inner derivative.
> Next

quiz 3 | ∫₀^(π/2) cos x dx = ?
* 1
o 0
o π/2
o −1
= sin(π/2) − sin 0.
> Next

quiz 3 | ∫ x√(x² + 1) dx = ?
* (1/3)(x² + 1)^(3/2) + C
o (2/3)(x² + 1)^(3/2) + C
o ½(x² + 1)^(1/2) + C
o x²√(x² + 1) + C
= u = x² + 1: ½ ∫ √u du = (1/3)u^(3/2).
> Next

quiz 3 | ∫₁⁴ 1/√x dx = ?
* 2
o 4
o 1
o 3
= [2√x]₁⁴ = 4 − 2.
> Next

quiz 3 | ∫ (eˣ + e⁻ˣ) dx = ?
* eˣ − e⁻ˣ + C
o eˣ + e⁻ˣ + C
o 2eˣ + C
o eˣ·e⁻ˣ + C
= That's 2 sinh x + C.
> Next

quiz 4 | ∫ cos²x dx = ?
* x/2 + sin(2x)/4 + C
o cos³x/3 + C
o x/2 − sin(2x)/4 + C
o sin²x + C
= Use cos²x = (1 + cos 2x)/2.
> Next

quiz 3 | Average value of sin x on [0, π]?
* 2/π
o 1/2
o 1
o 0
= (1/π)∫₀^π sin x dx = 2/π.
