## c2-px3 | Calc 2 drill | maths | 2 | calc2 | c2-px2
quiz 3 | ∫ x eˣ dx = ?
* eˣ(x − 1) + C
o x eˣ + C
o eˣ(x + 1) + C
o x²eˣ/2 + C
= Parts with u = x.
> Next

quiz 3 | ∫ 1/(x² − 1) dx = ?
* ½ ln|(x − 1)/(x + 1)| + C
o ln|x² − 1| + C
o arctan x + C
o ½ ln|(x + 1)/(x − 1)| + C
= Partial fractions: ½[1/(x − 1) − 1/(x + 1)].
> Next

quiz 2 | Sum of the geometric series 2 + 1 + ½ + ¼ + …?
* 4
o 3
o ∞
o 8
= a/(1 − r) = 2/(1/2).
> Next

quiz 3 | Does Σ 1/n³ converge?
* Yes
o No
o Only conditionally
= p-series with p = 3 > 1. (Its value, ζ(3), is called Apéry's constant.)
> Next

quiz 3 | Does Σ 2ⁿ/n! converge?
* Yes, to e² − 1 (from n = 1)
o No
o Only for even n
o Yes, to 2
= Ratio test gives 0. Σ from 0 is e².
> Next

quiz 3 | First three nonzero terms of the Maclaurin series of e^(2x)?
* 1 + 2x + 2x²
o 1 + 2x + x²
o 1 + x + x²/2
o 2 + 2x + x²
= Substitute 2x: 1 + 2x + (2x)²/2.
> Next

quiz 4 | lim x→0 (eˣ − 1 − x)/x² = ?
* 1/2
o 1
o 0
o ∞
= eˣ = 1 + x + x²/2 + …
> Next

quiz 3 | Interval of convergence of Σ xⁿ/n (including endpoints)?
* −1 ≤ x < 1
o −1 < x < 1
o −1 ≤ x ≤ 1
o All x
= At x = 1 it's the harmonic series (diverges); at x = −1, alternating harmonic (converges).
> Next

quiz 4 | Solve y′ = 2y with y(0) = 3.
* y = 3e^(2x)
o y = 2e^(3x)
o y = 3 + 2x
o y = e^(2x) + 3
= Exponential growth with rate 2.
> Next

quiz 4 | General solution of y″ − 4y = 0?
* Ae^(2x) + Be^(−2x)
o A cos 2x + B sin 2x
o (A + Bx)e^(2x)
o Ae^(4x)
= r² − 4 = 0, r = ±2: real roots, exponentials.
> Next

quiz 4 | Arc length of y = cosh x from 0 to 1?
* sinh 1 ≈ 1.175
o cosh 1
o 1
o e
= √(1 + sinh²x) = cosh x. ∫₀¹ cosh x dx = sinh 1.
> Next

quiz 3 | Polar curve r = 4 sin θ is a circle with radius…
* 2
o 4
o 1
o 8
= r² = 4r sin θ → x² + y² = 4y → x² + (y − 2)² = 4.
> Physics drills next

